      "writtenOn": "2023-09-19T12:17:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "There\u0027s a possible inconsistency here, in that `Cbb` holds a local `CBB` but `BigNum` holds a pointer to a heap `BIGNUM`.\n\n(Which in turn makes me worry -- are we sure that a plain `CBB` is safe in Rust?  Will it correctly survive moves?)",
      "revId": "823e775f4df70e739fe42b1ec36b47b8e548c008",
