        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 227,
      "author": {
        "id": 1958315
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-09-20T09:14:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e There\u0027s a possible inconsistency here...\n\nIt\u0027s true there\u0027s some inconsistency in terms of style, since `BIGNUM` is created with `BN_new()` returning a pointer to `BIGNUM` and `CBB` is created with `CBB_init()`. But internally both hold a pointer to a buffer on heap.\n\nWhy do you think the CBB here is unsafe?",
      "parentUuid": "d951b5ca_5eef88f1",
      "revId": "823e775f4df70e739fe42b1ec36b47b8e548c008",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
