      "writtenOn": "2023-09-20T15:17:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I was wondering about the moves too.\n\nIn C, if I wrote:\n\nCBB x \u003d ... ;\nCBB y \u003d x;\n\nAnd never do anything with x again, is y guaranteed to be a valid CBB?\n\nIf not, we probably want Cbb to contain a Box\u003cCBB\u003e.\n\nBTW - could we use CBB_init_fixed to simplify things?",
      "parentUuid": "81997434_a335c508",
      "revId": "823e775f4df70e739fe42b1ec36b47b8e548c008",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
